#GitHub workflow to teach the team
Everyone should use GitHub Desktop. Each person does this:
1. Clone the repository.
2. Pull main.
3. Create a branch.
4. Make one focused change.
5. Commit it.
6. Push the branch.
7. Open a pull request.
8. You review and merge it into main.
9. Everyone pulls main again before beginning another task.
Use these branch names:
feature/token-calculation
feature/canvas-theme-panel
fix/late-submission-bug
docs/update-user-stories
chore/setup-extension
Use these commit messages:
feat(extension): add theme selector
feat(tokens): calculate early-submission bonus
fix(auth): handle expired Canvas session
docs: add sprint one user stories
chore: configure linting